    <h2>Import Export Code (IEC)</h2>
    <p>The IEC is issued by India's Directorate General of Foreign Trade (DGFT) and is the base registration required to export from India. Every legitimate Indian export business holds one.</p>
    <p><strong>IEC Number:</strong> {{ site.registrations.iecNumber }}</p>

    <h2>APEDA registration</h2>
    <p>APEDA (Agricultural and Processed Food Products Export Development Authority) registration (RCMC — Registration-cum-Membership Certificate) applies to exporters of scheduled agricultural products. Ours covers our agricultural export lines.</p>
    <p><strong>APEDA RCMC Number:</strong> {{ site.registrations.apedaRcmcNumber }}</p>

    <h2>What we don't claim</h2>
    <p>Beyond IEC and APEDA, Green Plus EXIM does not hold or claim any other industry certification. If your import requires a specific certification we don't hold, tell us as early as possible in your inquiry — for some requirements we can arrange third-party verification per shipment; for others, we'll tell you honestly if we can't meet the requirement.</p>

    <h2>Verifying our documentation</h2>
    <p>{{ site.complianceChecklistCta }} We're also glad to provide our IEC and APEDA registration documents directly to a serious buyer as part of due diligence before a first order. See <a href="/blog/how-to-verify-an-indian-exporter-before-you-pay/">How to Verify an Indian Exporter Before You Pay</a> for a general checklist that applies whether you're evaluating us or anyone else.</p>
